session: ad5-finding-74-retraction

## Retraction first

My previous handoff `designer__ad5-regime-i-has-no-floor-and-informativeness-cannot-see-the-rc.md`
(now `.DONE`) argued the `Enabled && !Live && RC > 0` composite is reachable **by construction**.
**That is retracted.** Finding 74 (review doc `d61aa219`) shows why. The error inflated a defect, so
if any `AD1`–`AD8` text absorbed the frequency escalation, it should come back out.

The half of that handoff about **regime (i) having no floor** is unaffected and still stands.

## Why the state does not arise by construction

Saturation's capacity store is pre-populated from every resolvable scale target as step 1 of
`RunAnalysis`, before the analyzer input is built and `Analyze` is called — same cycle
(`internal/engines/saturation/engine_v2.go:39-53`). `LoadFromScaleTarget` writes a positive
`EffectiveCapacity` (`capacity_store.go:122-128`), and `resolveEffectiveMaxBatchedTokens` has no
zero-yielding path (`deployment_parser.go:281-302`): explicit flag → that value; chunked V1 → 8192;
chunked V0 → 2048; unchunked `MaxModelLen > 2048` → `MaxModelLen`; terminal unconditional → 2048.

The variant therefore lands in the store branch with `Reason = "P0-store"`
(`analyzer.go:421-424`, `types.go:27-31`), not `NoData`. `ResultIsInformative` returns true on the
first non-NoData/non-Error variant *anywhere* in the result, so a single priced variant makes the whole
result informative; liveness is stamped and `VG-up` keeps saturation. No window.

The state now additionally requires **every** variant's scale target to be missing or unresolvable —
degenerate, and a louder problem in its own right than the starvation it would enable.

## The design point that survives, and is the reason I am still writing to you

The asymmetry I described is real; only my claim about its *consequence* was wrong. Liveness is
decided on per-variant `Reason` (`analyzer_helpers.go:53-63`), while the RC that reaches the optimizer
is computed from `RoleCapacities` — which the scheduler-queue term can fill without touching a single
`VariantCapacity`. **Nothing in the code relates those two predicates.**

What currently prevents the mismatch from mattering is not a predicate. It is a *conservative sizing
estimate for brand-new variants*, added for an unrelated reason, whose own comment frames it as a
convenience:

> Provide a conservative capacity estimate so that brand-new variants with no live data or compatible
> siblings can still be considered for scale-up.

So the protection is **incidental**. An engine whose args don't parse to a token budget, a future gate
on `EffectiveCapacity`, or a change to that fallback reopens the gap silently — and the failure mode
is the `AD5` starvation, which is not obviously connected to the sizing estimate anyone would be
editing. If the Type 1 wants the property "a result carrying positive per-role demand is never pruned
as uninformative," that seems worth stating as an invariant rather than leaving it to hold by
coincidence. I am not proposing which side moves — that is your call.

